---
// InteriorShell — the main+sidebar body of an interior page.
//
// The template AGENTS.md describes: three equal columns with the article
// spanning two (1080px at the container's widest, the long-form cap) and the
// sidebar in the third, main first in source order. It was written twice,
// identically, for the blog post and practice-area routes; this is that grid
// lifted out so the third consumer doesn't write it a third time.
//
// It takes no props, and each omission is deliberate:
//
//   - The sidebar is a NAMED SLOT rather than a prop. The three sidebars are
//     different components with different prop shapes — PostSidebar takes
//     five, PracticeAreaSidebar two, AboutSidebar none — so a prop would force
//     this file to import all three. The grid has no business knowing which
//     one it is holding.
//
//   - The prose size is NOT a prop. A practice area runs 18px/30px and a blog
//     post 17px/29px; that difference is real and stays in each page's own
//     scoped <style>, on its own `__body` class. Which works because Astro
//     assigns a scope hash at the AUTHORING site, not the render site: a
//     <div class="prose pa__body"> written in the page keeps the page's hash
//     even though it renders inside this component's <article>, so the page's
//     scoped rule still matches it. No :global() needed.
//
//     (What still gets no hash at all is <Content />'s markdown output, which
//     is why .prose itself lives unscoped in global.css. Unchanged by this.)
//
//   - The background is NOT a prop. All three consumers are --white. Awards
//     gained `tone` only when /thank-you/ actually needed bone; add one here
//     the same way, when a consumer needs it, rather than shipping a branch
//     nothing takes.
//
// The class prefix is `.interior`, not the shorter `.pa` the practice-area
// route used: home/PracticeAreas.astro already has a `.pa__grid` of its own on
// a <ul>. Both are scoped so they never collided, but the name is ambiguous to
// anyone grepping for it.
---

<div class="interior section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="interior__grid">
      <article class="interior__main">
        <slot />
      </article>

      <slot name="sidebar" />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .interior {
    background: var(--white);
  }

  /* align-items: start keeps the sidebar at its own height rather than
     stretching its cards down a 2,000-word row. */
  .interior__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--section-gap);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .interior__main {
    grid-column: span 2;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1439px) {
    .interior__grid {
      gap: 56px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .interior__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .interior__main {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
